WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.850
For your next deliveries, you'll be
going here, here, here and here.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.690
This many?

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.190
You've got a problem?

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.780
This is me giving you a lighter load
since you're a rookie.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:12.570
Right.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.320
I'll be heading out now.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.070
Whatever you do, don't forget
to get those receipts stamped!

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.620
R-Right.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.000
Am I ever going to be done?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.750
Hey, rookie, could you be any slower?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.460
- Sorry!
- I don't believe it.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.800
You haven't even gotten through
half of your quota yet!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.010
What kind of plan do you have
for delivering this oxygen anyway?

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.390
- Or maybe you're just slacking off?
- I am not—

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.470
Oh well, what do I care?

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.470
Why don't you start
by picking up the pace?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.190
Here, I'm adding these, too.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.190
Huh?

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.900
I know you can do it!

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.520
Prove to me that
you haven't been slacking off, okay?

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.820
I see you're having a hard time, too, huh?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.900
Yeah.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.070
Talk about overwhelmed!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.960
EPISODE 2:
THE LIVER, ALCOHOL, AND PRIDE

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.920
Okay, let's get going.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.960
Sure. See ya.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:36.960
See ya.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.050
Th-That's a Macrophage.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.260
They're all so pretty.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.140
Huh?

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.060
What?

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.900
<i>Macrophage.</i>

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.230
<i>A type of White Blood Cell.</i>

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.400
<i>Catches and kills
foreign substances like bacteria,</i>

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.530
<i>while determining antigens
and information about immune responses.</i>

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.780
I have to kill more. More...

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.080
Oh my, so you're a Red Blood Cell.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.130
Y-Yes.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.920
I thought you were a bacterium!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.800
My sincerest apologies.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:27.350
Man, that Macrophage is exhausted, too.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.190
Next is the Mucosal Cell in the oral cavity.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.900
ORAL MUCOSAL EPITHELIUM

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.900
This way, huh?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.770
Mucosal Cell?
I've come to deliver your oxy—

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.280
It's on fire?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.070
<i>Mouth ulcer.</i>

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.950
<i>An inflammation inside of the mouth
or on the tongue.</i>

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.490
<i>When the lesions are round, shallow
and have a distinct border,</i>

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.080
<i>they are called "aphthous."</i>

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:54.790
<i>Often caused by stress, sleep deprivation
and lack of oral hygiene.</i>

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.000
A-Are you Mucosal Cell?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.960
<i>Oral mucosa.</i>

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.420
<i>The mucous membrane
lining the inside of the mouth.</i>

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.970
<i>Also known as the mirror
reflecting one's physical health.</i>

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.560
WORKFLOW MANUAL
FOR RED BLOOD CELLS

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.560
When this kind of thing happens...

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.980
DURING DELIVERIES,
TRANSFERAL OF THE OXYGEN
MUST BE YOUR TOP PRIORITY!

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.980
"Top priority"?

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:16.940
Your seal...

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.900
U-Um, th-this receipt...

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.860
Please stamp this receipt!

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.740
The receipt!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.880
<i>Don't worry about stuff like that!</i>

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:41.050
<i>All we need to do is suppress our emotions
and deliver oxygen in silence!</i>

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.050
No way can I do that.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.010
No way.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.510
- Run.
- What?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.970
The mouth ulcer ruptured.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:54.140
We'll soon be invaded by bacteria!

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:07.870
Stay away!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.580
Stay away from me!

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.660
White Blood Cell!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.540
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.590
That was uncalled for.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.300
Hey, don't be that way, Senpai.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.850
She's right. After all,
it was such a hassle getting here.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.690
Th-Thank you so much!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.560
You?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:42.900
We've met before.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.240
You remember me?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.150
Too bad.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.030
You get extra points for the glasses,
but you're too slim.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:55.200
I hear you! If only he was
just a little more macho-looking, right?

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.920
<i>Phagocytosis or Phagocytic Effects.</i>

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.890
<i>When Phagocytes, such as Monocytes,
Macrophages and Neutrophils</i>

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.480
<i>engulf bacteria and other foreign
substances, and break them down.</i>

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.740
This is your precious oxygen, right?

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.320
Don't ever let it go even if it kills you.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.280
R-Right!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.160
Not good!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.500
Hold onto something!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.970
What's going on?

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.350
We're being engulfed by water and povidone-iodine
from the damaged area! This is...

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.310
It's gargling!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:56.680
<i>Gargling.</i>

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.140
<i>To wash away bacteria and viruses
in the mouth,</i>

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.270
<i>preventing respiratory tract inflammation.
Various theories exist.</i>

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.150
<i>Povidone-iodine.</i>

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.740
<i>An antiseptic used in gargling solutions.</i>

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.820
<i>Though it has a unique scent,
it's highly effective as an antiseptic.</i>

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.040
- Where'd that come from?
- Jeez, that's gross.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.960
Good job hanging onto that oxygen.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.470
Y-Yes. Thank you very much.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.760
Hang in there, rookie.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.430
See you later, Glasses!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.100
Build up that body of yours!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.400
Hey, Glasses is totally staring at us!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.110
Do you think maybe he's smitten with Senpai?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.440
Save your breath, will you?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.990
Right!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.120
I'm so wiped.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:08:00.700
No rest since Day One.
How many rounds do we have to do in a day?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.620
I came this close to dying three times.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.960
I'm telling you, I can't take
much more of this job.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.750
Are you okay, rookies?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.880
Oh, good work, sirs!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.720
It's all right, stay seated. The stress is more intense
than usual today, so I bet it's a lot to take in, huh?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.930
Just my veteran's gut,
but a day like this, it's going to rain.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.060
Rain?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.520
Wh-What's this?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:28.360
Hey, simmer down. This is alcohol.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.980
<i>Alcohol.</i>

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.990
<i>Upon entering the body,
it has the effect of alleviating tension</i>

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:39.700
<i>by temporarily improving circulation and inducing
the secretion of dopamine and serotonin.</i>

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.410
Alcohol?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.710
You can count on this happening
after overwhelming stress.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.750
Sure, it improves the circulation,

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.460
but then the body absorbs more fat,
making the blood all viscous.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.550
At this rate, we'll be delivering alcohol
all over the body.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.680
The other cells are going to be pissed.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.390
This stupid job... This stupid job...

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.390
Why should we do it?
Give us some days off!

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.600
Give us a long weekend off!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:10.440
I didn't... I didn't become
a Red Blood Cell for this!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.570
Hey, hey, get a grip.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.780
You're not used to alcohol, huh?
No way around it! Come with me.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.750
Even we need a break sometimes, right?

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.080
How about we get some healing
and refresh ourselves?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.500
We're here.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.420
This is the liver.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:37.720
LIVER

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.470
<i>The liver.</i>

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.220
<i>An organ that performs
a wide variety of functions,</i>

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:41.890
<i>such as the synthesis, excretion
and detoxification of substances.</i>

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:46.600
Woo-hoo! I've always wanted to visit the liver!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.400
It sure is lively here.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.400
BLOOD ALLEY
BILE TOWN
FIRST AVENUE

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:53.230
Well, of course.
The liver is the largest organ in the body.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.530
Not only does it metabolize
the Big Three nutrients...

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:01.200
but it also handles all kinds of tasks
like producing bile and breaking down toxins.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.370
So, it's a really crucial organ, huh?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.960
Is this your first time, rookie?

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.460
Y-Yes.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:12.960
Normally, I get by just dealing
with oxygen and nutrients, so—

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:17.300
We'll show you how to really have fun in the liver.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.720
Hey! Why don't you detox with us,
Red Blood Cell gentlemen?

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.470
Come on, let's go!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.390
Jeez, just can't get enough of that, huh, Gramps?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.190
I'm coming! I'm coming!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.270
Um, what do you mean by "detox"?

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.360
I brought along some youngsters. It's their first time,
so send them some sweet young things, okay?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.740
Consider it done, since you're always
such good customers. This way, please.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.000
Some guests have arrived!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.460
Welcome!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.310
You youngsters don't hold back
with your reactions. Good for you!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.310
I-It's not like I'm reacting!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.730
Thank you for your patience!

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.320
We'll be seating you in groups of three!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:18.030
Hepatocytes, please take Table 3!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.610
Welcome, Red Blood Cells.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.530
Please refresh yourselves tonight.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>Hepatocytes.</i>

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.500
<i>Cells that make up 70 to 80% of the liver.</i>

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:35.420
<i>They metabolize and detoxify substances.</i>

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.880
- N-Nice to meet you.
- Is this your first time coming to a place like this?

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.840
Yes! It's our first time!

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:48.180
Wonderful, isn't it, rookie? Having a gorgeous
Hepatocyte like this help us detox!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.190
What do you mean by "detox"?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.480
Right, here you go.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.150
Huh? What's this?

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.980
This is ADH.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.780
ADH?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.860
That's right. It's an enzyme
that breaks down alcohol.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:03.950
<i>ADH.</i>

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.490
<i>An enzyme present in the Hepatocytes.</i>

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.450
<i>Has the ability to convert
alcohol into acetaldehyde.</i>

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.420
Alcohol is a substance
that triggers intoxication, right?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:20.050
It's our job as Hepatocytes to break down
and detoxify alcohol in the blood to sober you up.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.510
Oh, so that's what "detox" means.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.850
Goro can't dwink ADH by himself!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.220
Dwink?

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.350
What am I going to do with you?
Here, there you go!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.360
Don't cringe at me, dummy!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.150
When you're at a place like this,
just forget all about work and have a good time!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.280
R-Right.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.120
Forget all about work...

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.380
You really chugged that!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.840
- That was hot!
- For real?

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.010
Gimme a "That's a good boy!"

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.340
That's a good boy!

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.340
What's wrong?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.300
You have a frown on your face.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:09.970
It's nothing.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.680
You owe it to yourself to have some fun.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.850
He's right! Drink up and refresh yourself!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.020
Okay.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.280
That was great!
Good job downing that!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.990
I'm starting to feel queasy.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.990
I'm telling you, I can't take it!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.290
The blood vessels are so uneven,
trying to walk through them is a joke!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.620
The higher-ups aren't giving us
a second thought!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:40.790
Damn it! They have to improve
our working conditions or we can't go on!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.380
That's right!

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.130
Don't we even get paid time off?
Where's our paid time off?

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.800
Wh-What's that?
That black haze...

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.390
That's acetaldehyde.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.180
Huh?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:56.480
Acetaldehyde is what you get
when alcohol is metabolized by ADH.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:00.860
It's a powerful toxin,
but to eliminate alcohol completely,

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.440
you need to convert it
to this substance first.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.440
<i>Acetaldehyde.</i>

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:08.780
<i>A highly toxic substance.</i>

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.160
<i>Can also be found in automobile
exhaust fumes and tobacco smoke.</i>

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.200
A toxin?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.290
That's why everyone's pissed
and out of control.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.670
All right, the next step is...

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:23.710
What's that?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.220
An enzyme called "ALDH."

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.430
<i>ALDH.</i>

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:33.390
<i>An enzyme that metabolizes acetaldehyde
into acetic acid, detoxifying it.</i>

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:39.400
<i>Acetic acid is ultimately converted into water
and carbon dioxide, then expelled from the body.</i>

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.770
If you detoxify the acetaldehyde
by metabolizing it,

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.860
it will sober you up completely.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:49.660
Now, does everyone have a glass of ALDH?

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.950
Once again, let's raise a glass
to working healthy again tomorrow!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.200
Cheers!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.660
Cheers!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.330
<i>Transport the oxygen!</i>

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.600
How can I be in the mood to raise a glass?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.560
Can we just erase it all with this enzyme?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.770
All our suffering...

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.400
Rookie?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.200
Every day, all we do
is run around delivering oxygen.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.870
We're so easily replaceable.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:40.370
One or two drops of blood being shed
isn't going to affect this body in any way!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.130
Oh, don't talk like that.
In one go, all right?

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.420
What do you...

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.090
What do you people know about it?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.300
Aren't the internal organs and the bowels
where the elite work?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.510
A safe spot from where you can watch us
scrambling around?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.770
People like you with such carefree jobs...

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.480
You don't know anything about our pain!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.070
That's enough. You're a really bad drunk.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:11.700
Are you all right?

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.990
I'll bring you another glass right away.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:18.580
Rookie...

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.870
Come with me.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.830
Are you all right?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.550
I'm sorry.
There's been so much alcohol lately.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.550
Why don't you take a break?

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:32.840
I'll be fine.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:38.890
The other Hepatocytes have been hit hard by the
acetaldehyde toxins, but they're soldiering on.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.980
<i>Liver failure.</i>

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:46.110
<i>Overconsumption of alcohol
can lead to a fatty liver</i>

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:50.320
<i>due to acetaldehyde inhibiting
the breakdown of fats.</i>

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:56.780
<i>Chronic binging will eventually destroy
the liver cells, triggering hepatic cirrhosis.</i>

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.540
We're not the only ones who are suffering.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:07.000
The Red Blood Cells risk their lives
to work like crazy for us.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.710
As long as they're here,
I don't want them to see me being weak.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:19.350
I've seen all kinds of cells over the years,

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.310
but there isn't one single easy task
in this world.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.980
Well, I guess you've been through a lot.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:29.150
If an old geezer like me will do, talk to me.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.360
I...

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:32.900
I...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.990
I just ran off!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.910
Bailing on the job I was supposed to do...

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:43.910
Because of that, S-Senpai...

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:49.540
My only task is to deliver oxygen,
but I can't even get that right!

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.920
I'm not blaming you.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.420
The longer you live,
the more shame you suffer.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.760
I've been scrambling around myself,
just like you.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.520
That's how each and every one of us
eventually becomes a full-fledged cell.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.150
Right.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:13.480
The future of this world
rest on the shoulders of you youngsters.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.280
I'm counting on you, rookie.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.950
I'm really sorry.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.540
For being so rude to you just now.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.830
Don't worry about it. That's how harsh
the conditions you're fighting under are.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.500
Come detox yourself anytime, okay?

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.210
Okay! Thank you very much!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.840
Well, now we're refreshed.
Why don't we head out now?

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.840
Hey, come on. Let's go, Gramps.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.810
Gramps?

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.270
So, he's passed away.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.940
Thank you for your long years of hard work.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:58.990
No way.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.240
Take him to the sinusoid.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.010
Who's that?

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.340
That's the Kupffer Cell.

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:22.430
She devours Red Blood Cells
who've completed their missions.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:23.550
What?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.310
<i>Kupffer Cell.</i>

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.480
<i>A type of Macrophage
that exists in the sinusoid.</i>

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.520
<i>It activates by ingesting foreign particles.</i>

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:38.530
<i>Aging Red Blood Cells are also ingested
to produce bile pigment from hemoglobin.</i>

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.700
This is the life of a Red Blood Cell.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:48.000
We deliver oxygen until we die,
and we get used as nutrients afterwards.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:52.330
Still, it's not a bad way to go, is it?

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.210
Gramps...

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.420
sure did look content.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.060
Goodbye, rookie.
I'll be waiting for you.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:12.810
Okay!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.780
Good luck at work.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.450
White Blood Cell!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.410
Oh hey, it's not what you...

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.870
I came to patrol the fatty liver.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.790
It could trigger cirrhosis
if we just leave it.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:37.960
O-Oh, is that right?

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.090
Come to think of it, seems like
a lot of alcohol rained down.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.260
Are you all right?

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:46.430
Yes. Um, thanks to Hepatocyte.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.510
I see.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.350
But don't let your guard down.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.900
Hey, you rookies, are you okay?

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.230
I feel sick.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:02.700
Not all of the acetaldehyde
got broken down, huh?

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.700
<i>Hangover.</i>

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.910
<i>While traces of acetaldehyde
remain in the body,</i>

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:14.000
<i>its toxins trigger headaches and nausea.</i>

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.830
You know this doesn't mean
that you can take a break, right?

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:19.590
We know.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:23.550
All right, deliver that oxygen!
Take Gramps's share with you!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.760
- Right!
- Right!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.260
<i>There are all kinds of jobs in this world.</i>

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.970
<i>I want to see it through.</i>

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.980
<i>By becoming a full-fledged Red Blood Cell.</i>

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.850
Huh? Alcohol?

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.980
Come on! Again?

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.980
<i>Hair of the dog.</i>

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:46.030
<i>Long touted as a remedy for easing hangover
symptoms, though there is no scientific basis for this.</i>

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:51.410
<i>It can be assumed that one is only gaining relief from
headaches and nausea thanks to being intoxicated.</i>

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.500
PREVIEW

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:23.130
Due to this body
engaging in sexual reproduction...

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.380
it is now in a state of arousal.

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:25.380
EXCITEMENT

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:28.220
Go off and become men!

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:28.220
EXPANSION

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:30.340
EMPTINESS

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:32.720
Why were they ever born in this world, then?

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:34.010
EXCITEMENT, EXPANSION, AND EMPTINESS
